        <p>
          While the Central Government mandates DA indexation and HRA city classifications for central civil servants, defence personnel, and railways, state administrations across <strong>Tamil Nadu</strong>, <strong>Uttar Pradesh</strong>, <strong>Maharashtra</strong>, <strong>Rajasthan</strong>, <strong>Bihar</strong>, and <strong>Karnataka</strong> adapt these structures through their respective State Pay Revision Committees.
        </p>
        <p>
          State finance departments evaluate central guidelines and release localized Government Orders (G.O.) mapping state cities—such as classifying Chennai, Lucknow, Mumbai, and Bengaluru into Tier-1 brackets and district headquarters into Tier-2 or Tier-3 brackets. Consequently, the calculations provided by our DA HRA tool serve as a critical analytical roadmap for millions of civil servants, police personnel, and government teachers across India.
        </p>
